:: Fishing Pier Catch
<<effects>>
<<if $daily.fishing.pier.whitney.phase is "bet">>
	<<fishingPierCaughtWhitneyBet>>
<<elseif $daily.fishing.pier.whitney.phase is "idle" and $rng gte 90 and !$daily.fishing.pier.whitney.fishKiss>>
	<<set $daily.fishing.pier.whitney.fishKiss to true>>
	<<fishingPierCaughtWhitneyKiss>>
<<elseif $daily.fishing.pier.fisher.phase is "fishing" and $daily.fishing.pier.fisher.drunk gte 4 and $rng gte 80>>
	<<fishingPierCaughtFisherDrunk>>
<<elseif Weather.dayState is "day" and [undefined, "finished"].includes($daily.fishing.pier.whitney.phase) and [undefined, "finished"].includes($daily.fishing.pier.fisher.phase) and $rng gte 90 and $daily.fishing.seagullSteal is undefined>>
	<<fishingSeagullCaught $fishingHookedFish $bus>>
<<else>>
	<<fishingPierCaught>>
<</if>>


:: Fishing Pier Reel
<<effects>>
<<set $fishingReelAttempts += 1>>
<<if $athleticsSuccess>>
	You brace against the rocks and heave, and you <<if $fishingReelAttempts gt 1>>finally<</if>> <span class="green">reel up the fish.</span><<gtiredness>><<tiredness 1>>
	<br><br>

	<<include "Fishing Pier Catch">>
<<elseif $fishingReelAttempts gte 3 and random(1, 5) gte 4>>
	<<if $daily.fishing.pier.whitney.phase is "bet">>
		<<fishingPierLineSnappedWhitneyBet>>
	<<elseif $rng gte 80>>
		<<if $daily.fishing.pier.fisher.phase is "fishing" and random(1, 2) is 1>>
			<<fishingPierPulledInFisherSaved>>
		<<elseif $daily.fishing.pier.whitney.phase is "idle">>
			<<fishingPierPulledInWhitney>>
		<<else>>
			<<fishingPierPulledIn>>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif $rng gte 60>>
		<<fishingPierRodLost>>
	<<else>>
		<<fishingPierLineSnapped>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if $fishingReelAttempts is 1>>
		You haul back on your rod, but the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> strips your line right back off the reel. Your arms burn with the effort.<<gtiredness>><<tiredness 1>>
	<<else>>
		You drag it closer, close enough to see its shape beneath the dark water, before it dives again, wrenching you against the railing.<<gtiredness>><<tiredness 1>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<set _reelDifficultyMax to Math.clamp($fishingHookedFish.size * 10, 600, 1400)>>
	<<link [[Keep fighting it|Fishing Pier Reel]]>><</link>><<athleticsdifficulty -250 _reelDifficultyMax>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Cut the line|Fishing Pier Cut Line]]>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: Fishing Pier Cut Line
<<effects>>
You release the tension on your rod, letting your line go slack. The <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> pulls harder, and with a sudden snap, your line breaks free. Through the dark water below, you catch a glimpse of it darting away.
<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
<br><br>

<<if $daily.fishing.pier.whitney.phase is "bet">>
	<<fishingPierCutLineWhitneyBet>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Re-hook the line and cast back out (0:03)|Fishing Pier Wait]]>><<pass 3>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Dock Pier]]>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: Widgets Fishing Pier Catch [widget]
<<widget "fishingPierPulledInFisherSaved">>
	<<loadNPC 0 "fishing_pier_npc_fisher">><<person1>>
	You lean back with everything you have left, but the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> pulls harder. <span class="red">You're hauled over the railing,</span> but the <<person>> next to you grabs you before you can be pulled in. Your rod slips from your hands and disappears into the sea.<<gstress>><<stress 3>><<handheldruined>>
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<<run stopFishingProp()>>
	<br><br>

	"You okay?" <<he>> asks, breathing hard.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Fishing Pier Fisher Saved On Pier]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Thank with a kiss|Fishing Pier Fisher Thank Kiss]]>><<set $phase to 1>><<promiscuous1>><<kissvirginitywarning>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishingPierPulledIn">>
	You lean back with everything you have left, but the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> pulls harder. <span class="red">You're dragged over the railing and into the water below,</span> your rod torn from your hands as you fall.<<gstress>><<stress 5>><<handheldruined>>
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<<run stopFishingProp()>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Sea Docks]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishingPierRodLost">>
	You lean back with everything you have left, but the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> gives one last violent pull and your rod is wrenched clean out of your hands, clattering over the railing into the sea.<<gstress>><<stress 4>><<handheldruined>>
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<<run stopFishingProp()>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Return to fishing|Fishing Pier Wait]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Dock Pier]]>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishingPierLineSnapped">>
	You lean back with everything you have left, but your line goes taut, then <span class="red">snaps.</span> The <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> is gone, and your line goes slack.
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<<run stopFishingProp()>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Re-hook the line and cast back out (0:03)|Fishing Pier Wait]]>><<pass 3>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Dock Pier]]>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishingPierCaught">>
	<<set _canEatFish to canEatFishTf($fishingHookedFish)>>
	<<run updateFishRecord($fishingHookedFish.type, $fishingHookedFish.size, $bus)>>
	<<run stopFishingProp()>>
	<<set _fishPropName to "caught-" + $fishingHookedFish.type>>
	<<wearProp _fishPropName>>

	<<fishingCatchFishText $fishingHookedFish>>
	<br><br>

	<<if $fishingHookedFish.size gte 100 and Time.dayState is "day" and $docks.hired and $rng gte 80>>
		In the distance, dock workers notice the size of it and a couple cheer for you from the docks.<<dockstatus 1>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<if _canEatFish>>
		It's such a small fish, you could probably fit the whole thing in your mouth.
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Stow it away|Fishing Pier Keep]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [["Throw the " + $fishingHookedFish.type + " back"|Fishing Pier Throw Back]]>><</link>>
	<<if _canEatFish>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Eat the fish|Fishing Pier Cat Eat]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>
